WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.152
The first major question is how the dataset is organized.

00:00:03.152 --> 00:00:05.927
Structured data follows a predefined schema.

00:00:05.927 --> 00:00:10.162
Semi-structured data has named fields but allows flexibility and nesting.

00:00:10.162 --> 00:00:13.892
Unstructured data does not naturally arrive as rows and columns.

00:00:13.892 --> 00:00:16.472
These categories describe organization.

00:00:16.472 --> 00:00:22.192
A structured table can still have missing values, duplicate records, or poorly defined variables.

00:00:22.192 --> 00:00:24.967
Organization and quality are separate issues.

00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:30.962
Connect this idea to a hospital combining patient tables, device JSON, and clinical notes.

00:00:30.962 --> 00:00:35.787
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:35.787 --> 00:00:42.687
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:42.687 --> 00:00:47.642
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:47.642 --> 00:00:52.480
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
